    "source": "// Wasm-tier example (backends/wasm): i32-only services, no host builtins.\n// Beacon writes its presence into a kv coeffect (with inverses) and provides\n// a status service; Auditor snapshots the status into kv when it activates.\n// The kv provider itself is not written in revl — in the demo it is a\n// hand-written WAT component (a polyglot mesh: the runtime neither knows\n// nor cares which language produced which component).\n\nservice Kv {\n  fn get(k: Int) -> Int\n  fn set(k: Int, v: Int)\n}\n\nservice Status {\n  fn shared() -> Int\n}\n\ncomponent Beacon requires kv: Kv provides status: Status {\n  effect kv.set(7, 100) undo kv.set(7, 0)\n  effect kv.set(8, 200) undo kv.set(8, 0)\n\n  provide status {\n    fn shared() = kv.get(7)\n  }\n}\n\ncomponent Auditor requires status: Status, kv: Kv {\n  effect kv.set(9, status.shared()) undo kv.set(9, 0)\n}\n"
